course: dictionary
lesson: 6458
title: Words about boats and canals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A narrowboat is a long, thin boat. You can work out its meaning from its name, because narrow means thin and a boat is a boat. «Narrowboats are only about 2 metres wide, to fit the narrow locks.» The clues are narrow and locks: the boat is built to be slim enough for the narrow canals and their locks.
explain: The sentence also says that «many boat families lived in a tiny cabin at the back». So a narrowboat can be a home as well as a boat. Words can have more than one use, and the other words around them show which one the writer means.
fact: A narrowboat is about 2 metres wide and up to 22 metres long.
fact: Narrowboats were made to travel on the narrow canals of Britain.
fact: In the 1700s and 1800s, horses walked along the towpath and pulled narrowboats full of coal and goods.
fact: Many families lived in a tiny cabin at the back of a narrowboat, often painted with roses and castles.
fact: Today many people live on narrowboats or hire them for holidays. Canals have locks and deep water, so always stay safe.
exercise: «Narrowboats are only about 2 metres wide, to fit the narrow locks.» What does narrow mean here? | Full of water | *Thin, not wide | Very old | Very loud
exercise: In the 1700s and 1800s, what pulled narrowboats along the canals? | Children on bicycles | *Horses walking along the towpath | Strong winds from the sea | Sails made of cloth
exercise: What is a narrowboat used for? | A tall ship crossing the ocean | *A floating home or a holiday boat | A boat for deep sea fishing | A train that runs on water
test: «Many boat families lived in a tiny cabin at the back.» What does tiny mean? | Very noisy | *Very small | Very tall | Very dark
test: Why must a narrowboat be so narrow? | To carry more people on top | To go faster in the sea | To float on snow | *To fit the narrow canals and locks
exam: Which statement about narrowboats is true? | They were first made last year | *They can be used as floating homes | They travel only on the open sea | They are over 30 metres long
